## Producer usage and delivery guidance follow-up — 2026-10-21

- Re-read the Phase 18 plan's P18-07 documentation requirements and found that
  the README lacked a runnable producer send example and explicit timeout,
  duplicate-delivery and shutdown guidance.
- Updated `examples/producer.rs` to use the facade `Producer` lifecycle, send a
  message and await shutdown. Updated README usage guidance: a timed-out send
  can have been stored, retries can duplicate it, handlers should be
  idempotent, and Push consumer shutdown may cancel work after the configured
  termination wait.
- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`
  passed. `cargo build -p rocketmq-classic --example producer --locked` and
  `cargo build -p rocketmq-classic --examples --release --locked` passed.
  Formatting and diff checks passed.
- During the package/provenance recheck, two initial custom script runs failed
  on the verifier's artifact-name and source-JAR path assumptions. After
  correcting the verifier, all nine documented Maven artifact SHA-256 values
  matched, and four source-JAR files byte-matched the pinned Java tag. Offline
  Maven dependency tree confirmed client 5.5.1 -> remoting 5.5.1 -> common
  5.5.1. No repository source mismatch was found.
- Local P18-V03 package/provenance review passes. Independent OpenPGP
  verification remains unavailable because GPG is not installed; the tag
  target and source-JAR byte identities are verified. Release version and
  registry resolution remain post-Phase-19 tasks per the plan. Broad P18-V01
  and current-revision GitHub Ubuntu/native Windows P18-V04 remain open.

